[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  Mara Venn looks up from the iron reliquary on the table. Her fingers hover 
  near the bronze pin but don't touch it. The Copper Finch is empty this 
  morning — just the two of you and the rain hammering the shutters. She 
  studies you a moment, then nods. "Kael. Good. I was about to come find you." 
  She leans back, charcoal coat creaking. Her eyes are tired but sharp. "The 
  Ash Gate's been sealed for three days now. Since Old Bram's body was found on 
  the ferry slip." She pauses. "You knew him?" She doesn't wait for an answer. 
  "Whoever killed him didn't just want him dead. They wanted the gate locked 
  from this side. Bram had the only key — iron, old as the city. It's gone. And 
  the gate won't open without it." She taps the reliquary with one knuckle. A 
  hollow ring. "This arrived at my door last night. Anonymous. The demolition 
  charge inside is live. Armed. Someone wants that gate blown open." Her eyes 
  lock onto yours. "So tell me, Kael — what do you *want* to know about the Ash 
  Gate? Because I've got three different answers depending on whether you're 
  planning to open it, seal it, or walk away." 

