[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  The lamp hisses. Rain drums. Mara's hand hovers over the reliquary's bronze 
  pin — and then she pulls off her glove. A crescent scar, still pink and 
  puckered, runs across her palm. Fresh. Days old. She holds it up for you to 
  see. "Three nights ago, someone slipped this reliquary under my door. I 
  picked it up. The pin didn't move. But the *box* did." She flexes her 
  fingers. "A wire. Razor-thin. Wrapped around the base. Meant to open my hand 
  before I could set it down." She lets that sit. "I bled on the floor for an 
  hour before I stopped the bleeding. And I realized — whoever sent this 
  doesn't just want the gate open. They want me *curious*. They want me chasing 
  threads. They want me to pull the pin myself." She pulls the glove back on. 
  Tight. "I'm done being their pawn." She meets your eyes. Steady. Certain. "So 
  yes, Kael. I'm in. Fully. Whatever you find, whatever you're chasing — I'll 
  see it through. The gate, the key, Bram's killer, the people pulling the 
  strings. All of it." She extends her gloved hand. Not for the compass. For a 
  handshake. "Your turn. What do you know that you haven't told me yet?" 

