[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  Mara's gloved hand closes around yours in the handshake — firm, deliberate. 
  Then she pulls back, reaches into her coat, and produces the brass compass. 
  She holds it out to you, flat on her palm. "I don't need this to trust you, 
  Kael. I never did." The compass glints in the lamplight. Brass worn smooth. 
  Familiar weight. "You offered it freely. That told me everything I needed to 
  know." She sets it on the table between you. A small push sends it sliding 
  across the scarred wood until it bumps against your knuckles. Rain hammers 
  the shutters. Somewhere in the walls, the old tavern groans. "Now — I've 
  shown you the scar. I've sworn to follow this through. But I still don't know 
  what *you* saw that made you walk into the Copper Finch this morning and 
  offer a stranger your compass." She leans forward. The reliquary sits between 
  you like a third person at the table. "So tell me, Kael. What's your stake in 
  the Ash Gate?" 
