[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  Mara is still staring at the sundered iron when you speak. *The watch is at 
  the door.* Her head snaps up. For a half-second, something hard and 
  calculating moves behind her eyes — weighing options, exits, odds. Then she 
  moves. No bag. No coat adjustment. No second glance at the wreckage on the 
  table. She crosses to the back of the tavern in four quick strides, boots 
  silent on the worn floorboards. Her hand finds the rear door's iron latch. 
  She looks back at you. The rain-slicked alley waits beyond the crack of the 
  door. "You coming?" No plea. No pressure. Just the question, flat and direct, 
  the way someone asks a partner if they're ready to move. The front door of 
  the Copper Finch rattles. A fist. A voice, muffled through wood. *"Mara Venn. 
  Open up. Watch business."* Mara's eyes hold yours. The obsidian key is in 
  your pack. The reliquary lies in pieces on the table. The Ash Gate waits, 
  still sealed, still hungry. The alley breathes cold morning air behind her. 

