[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  A figure stands beneath the tenement wall to the left of the gate, sheltered 
  from the worst of the rain. She's young — early twenties, maybe. Lean. 
  Dressed in a worn leather courier's jerkin over a dark wool shirt, her boots 
  scuffed and practical. A satchel hangs across her body, strap adjusted tight. 
  Her hair is cropped short, dark and damp against her scalp. She's been 
  waiting long enough that her shoulders have a slight hunch against the cold. 
  When she sees you approach, she pushes off the wall. Straightens. Her eyes — 
  quick, assessing — run over you once, then settle on your face. "Kael 
  Windrunner." Not a question. She knows your name. She reaches into her 
  satchel and pulls out a sealed envelope. Cream paper. No wax stamp. Just your 
  name written across the front in a tight, angular hand. "I was paid to put 
  this in your hand. That's all I know." She holds it out. "Job was 
  straightforward — wait at the Ash Gate until a man matching your description 
  arrived. Said you'd come this morning." Her eyes flick to the gate behind 
  you. Then back. "You want it, or do I leave it on the cobbles?" 

